// package-template main — a library package, so there is no program
// here.
//
// A manifest names an entry point whether or not anything runs it, and
// a dependency's entry point is never built.  This file exists to be
// that name and to say what to do instead.
//
// A package that IS a program puts the program here, and everything the
// program is made of in modules beside this file.

fn main() [io]
    println("package-template: a library — depend on it and `use template`")
